      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">The logic followed here is:</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Given word:&nbsp;ACQUIRE</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, arranged in reversed alphabetical order:</p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); width: 400px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Word</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>A</strong></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>C</strong></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Q</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">U</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">I</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>R</b></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">E</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Alphabetical order</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>A</strong></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>C</strong></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">E</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">I</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Q</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>R</b></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">U</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Here, &#39;<strong>Three</strong>&#39;&nbsp;&nbsp;letters &#39;<strong>A C R</strong>&#39; will remain unchanged if each of the letters in the word <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">ACQUIRE&nbsp;</span>is arranged in alphabetical order.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Hence, the correct answer is&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">&quot;Option 1&quot;</span>.</p>\n",
